<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iberia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Iberian Peninsula, Iberian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iberia, or the Iberian Peninsula, is the south-western peninsula of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, comprising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and Portugal. It was a major arena for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> and later ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a>. It was also the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Portuguese and Spanish overseas empires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iberia.jpg" alt="Iberia" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacques Descloitres, MODIS Rapid Response Team, NASA/GSFC · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Espa%C3%B1a_y_Portugal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
